  Persistence:-  in LangGraph means saving the information or state of a workflow so that it is not lost when
  the workflow stops, pauses, or the application restarts. LangGraph saves the current state as a checkpoint,
  which is basically a saved snapshot of the workflow at a particular point. Later, LangGraph can load that
  checkpoint and continue the workflow from where it stopped instead of starting from the beginning.
  Persistence is especially useful for chat applications, long-running workflows, human approval workflows,
  and failure recovery. In simple terms, persistence is like a save feature in a game—it saves the progress
  of your LangGraph workflow so you can continue it later.

  Persistence not only save the end state but it also saved the middle/intermediate values of state.
  if workflow get crashed, as intermediate state are saved , instead of staring the workflow from start start it from where it stops
  also called as folt tolerance

